--- TURN 1 ---
Fixed. The bug was classic mutable-default-argument state leaking: `add_item(item, cart=[])` and `add_tagged(item, tags=[], extra={})` created their default list/dict once at def time, so every call with no explicit container shared the same objects.

Changes in `cart.py` (public API and call signatures unchanged — callers can still pass explicit list/dict or nothing):
- `add_item(item, cart=None)` — creates a fresh `[]` when `cart is None`
- `add_tagged(item, tags=None, extra=None)` — creates fresh `[]`/`{}` when either is `None`
- Updated the module docstring that advertised the bug

Verification: `uv run --with pytest pytest test_cart.py -q` (system python3 has no pytest; project is PEP 668-managed, so I ran it via uv without creating new files) → 3 passed. `test_cart.py` untouched.

